    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented for the owner soft-delete change:\n\n## Changes\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `Owner.java`\n- Added a `deleted` boolean column (mirroring the existing primitive-boolean flags like `possibleDuplicate`) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. A new owner defaults to `false`.\n\n**Service** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.java`\n- `deleteOwner(...)` now flags `deleted = true` and `save`s instead of removing the row, so the record is retained and still readable via `findOwnerById`.\n- The three create-time duplicate/identity checks now skip soft-deleted owners: `existsOwnerWithIdentityKey` (identity duplicate), `findHouseholdMembers` (backs the household-duplicate check `existsOwnerInHousehold`, and consistently the household-size count), and `findPossibleDuplicateOwnerId` (soft-match). Each gained a single `.filter(existing -> !existing.isDeleted())`, keeping the logic where it already lived.\n\n**API contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically. GET therefore returns `deleted` (false for new owners, true after deletion).\n\n**Schema** \u2014 `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`\n- Added a `deleted BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (ddl-auto is `none`, so the schema files are authoritative). Seed inserts use explicit column lists and leave it NULL, consistent with the other primitive-boolean flags.\n\n## Verification\nThe full suite is green:\n- `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` \u2014 GET shows `deleted:false`, then `deleted:true` after DELETE, with the row retained.\n- `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` \u2014 recreating an owner whose only match was soft-deleted succeeds.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
